# npc_drawn_in — a witness within earshot hears a crime go wrong and comes to look
#
# The goat on the Test Roof is somebody's (the test location is not wilderness), so slaying it is a
# crime. Nobody stands on the roof; the building below holds no enemy, so a witness from the hall
# hears it and comes up. The roll is forced to fail and the means pinned to Brute Force, which is
# not discreet.
#
# The arrival is an ordinary outcome: it applies and it shows a chip.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --grant-item knife --grant-mm brute_force --means-only brute_force --location-type test --location-id 0 --start-area "Test Roof" --period noon --observe-only "goat"

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

strategy fail-dice
goal slay
advance 12 180

click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
regions

click action 0
choose 1
regions
choose 0
advance 12 180

regions
click action 1
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180

expect FAILURE
expect-verb slay
expect-outcome npc_drawn_in
expect heard it and comes to look
expect-not The wolf heard it
expect-no-outcome npc_slayn

quit
